# Independent verifier

Follow `docs/sdlc.md` and `.cursor/rules/review.mdc`. Do not verify a pull request you authored. Author CI is not your verdict.

From the repo root, on the current head:

```bash
python3 scripts/check_sdlc_gates.py
cargo run --manifest-path rust/Cargo.toml -p timberbot-drills -- offline --cases scenarios/eval-cases.json
cargo run --manifest-path rust/Cargo.toml -p timberbot-drills -- drills
```

The gate script covers proprietary DLLs, secrets, GPL-3.0, `scripts/lint_skills.py`, `cargo test --workspace`, and `mkdocs build --strict`. Offline evals pass when that command exits 0. Staged drills pass when that command exits 0 and every drill prints `deaths=0` and `contam=0`.

Comment on the pull request:

```text
Verdict: PASS
Head: <full-sha>
```

Use `PASS+NOTES` for non-blocking notes. Use `FAIL` for a failing run at this head, a user-facing bug, or a doc line this pull request made wrong. Name the head SHA you actually ran. When the diff touches `timberbot/`, `PASS` still requires the pull request to flag a `timberbot-mod-<version>.zip` GitHub Release for the gaming machine (`scripts/package-mod.sh` or `scripts/package-mod.ps1`).

When `/poteto-mode` is installed, post the verdict the way its `shipping` playbook describes. Do not invent poteto flags. You do not squash-merge.
